WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
A customer is ready to sign.

00:00:02.595 --> 00:00:04.240
Then comes one question.

00:00:05.055 --> 00:00:06.960
Can we see your SOC 2 report?

00:00:07.335 --> 00:00:09.380
Saying you're secure isn't enough.

00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:11.560
Show the controls.

00:00:12.015 --> 00:00:12.890
Show the owners.

00:00:13.255 --> 00:00:14.130
Show the evidence.

00:00:14.435 --> 00:00:15.980
AiVRIC Enterprise Vision.

00:00:16.335 --> 00:00:18.040
That's how trust moves forward.

00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:21.440
Start with scope.

00:00:21.535 --> 00:00:24.060
Security, availability, processing
integrity,

00:00:24.395 --> 00:00:26.040
confidentiality, and privacy.

00:00:26.615 --> 00:00:29.180
Know which trust categories your program
needs to address.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.268
Connect the controls.

00:00:31.343 --> 00:00:32.523
Map your baseline to SOC 2.

00:00:32.543 --> 00:00:35.368
See who owns each control, and which
requirements it supports.

00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:38.508
Close the gaps.

00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:40.368
Give each fix an owner and a deadline.

00:00:40.443 --> 00:00:41.988
Keep it moving until the work is done.

00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:46.448
Make risk decisions accountable.

00:00:46.603 --> 00:00:49.163
Record the approval, the safeguards, and the
expiry,

00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:51.468
so an accepted risk doesn't become a
forgotten risk.

00:00:52.463 --> 00:00:53.723
Keep incident response on record.

00:00:53.743 --> 00:00:56.708
Declare, triage, contain, recover, and
close.

00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:59.068
Every step becomes part of the incident's
history.

00:01:00.063 --> 00:01:01.208
Make evidence verifiable.

00:01:01.263 --> 00:01:03.328
Follow the actions on a hash-chained audit
trail.

00:01:03.543 --> 00:01:06.088
Check the chain and give your auditor a
record they can verify.

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:08.608
Then share the proof.

00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:11.528
Put your independent auditor's SOC 2 report
in your trust center.

00:01:11.623 --> 00:01:15.068
Give customers access by request while
keeping raw findings private.

00:01:15.943 --> 00:01:18.228
Type II examines how controls operate over
time.

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:20.048
Build the evidence as the work happens,

00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:22.028
so your team is ready when the auditor asks.

00:01:22.817 --> 00:01:23.692
One organization.

00:01:23.997 --> 00:01:26.137
Clear ownership across business units and
regions.

00:01:26.157 --> 00:01:27.822
One connected program.

00:01:29.707 --> 00:01:31.192
AiVRIC Enterprise Vision.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:32.047
See it.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:32.707
Score it.

00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:33.447
Prove it.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.912
Book your SOC 2 walkthrough.
